I wrote for years as **OJ Develops** on Blogger. Free hosting, low friction — but as a job-hunting and portfolio surface it fights back. Themes are awkward to customize, and the brand was never as clear as just using my name.

So this is the new home: **ojraqueno.com** — a static Astro site, posts editable in a local admin UI (Keystatic), published by committing to git.

## What stays the same

- The voice and the kinds of topics
- Older posts, migrated with their **original publish dates**
- A clear note on each migrated post linking back to Blogger

## What changes

- Brand is my name, aligned with GitHub and LinkedIn
- Look and feel we control
- Posts and companion GitHub repos treated as one portfolio
- A steadier cadence aimed at .NET backend, full-stack, and design tradeoffs — including how AI fits into real engineering work

If you still have the Blogger RSS bookmarked, keep it for a while. New writing lands here first.
